			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2459530">
									

<p>There's a limit to how much comedically misspelled, Spanko-style interviews I can enjoy, and I think I've reached it. It feels as though there are two dave-templates operating at the moment, one of which finishes with a short interview log which establishes a single character trait, usually for comedic effect (this one, 2324, 4055-J, 2527, 3V1L-J, TTKU-J, SCP-J) and the other of which uses escalating lists for comedic effect (WTF-J, 7000-J). 2219 and 2416 combine both templates. Many of the shorter-lived SCPs also fall into one of these camps.</p>
<p>That's not to say that the templates aren't effective. They are, and there are some good writing techniques at work in each of them. And they clearly work for the up-voting audience. It's just become a bit predictable for me - there's only so many times I can see the same trick done well and still be impressed.</p>

